WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
JENNY BROWN: Today we're talking
about sustainability, Spanner,

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.800
a compute GA, and live
Q&amp;A. I'm Jenny Brown,

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.990
and welcome to
This Week in Cloud,

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:14.310
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.700
Google Cloud aims to
be carbon free by 2030.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.760
We measure our progress along
this path with our carbon

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.890
free energy percentage,
which is now

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.010
public for the majority of
our Google Cloud regions.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:29.670
We're sharing this data because
just like latency or cost,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.260
we hope that carbon
emissions will

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.280
factor into your decision
making when moving to the Cloud.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.490
Cloud Spanner recently launched
a point-in-time recovery

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.890
capability that
provides complete data

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.160
protection against inadvertent
deletion or updates

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.900
due to user error.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.560
With this capability, Spanner
now offers continuous data

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.800
protection with the ability
to recover your past data

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.410
to a microsecond granularity.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.500
This helps enterprises
quickly fix data corruption

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.020
to reduce risk,
loss of business,

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.599
and minimize impact on
customer experience.

00:01:04.599 --> 00:01:08.910
We're excited to announce the
general availability of A2 VMs

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:12.060
based on the Nvidia
Ampere A1 tensor core

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.370
GPUs in Compute Engine.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.580
This is going to enable
customers around the world

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.180
to run their Nvidia
CUDA-enabled ML and HPC

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:25.890
scale-out and scale-up workloads
more efficiently and at a lower

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:26.820
cost.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.040
Check out the post
for a full rundown

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.190
of how our A2 VMs stand apart.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.860
Did you miss the first
Ask Google Cloud?

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.800
Catch up with the recording
of the live Q&amp;A session

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.200
all about serverless
architectures,

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.720
and don't forget to submit
your questions on Twitter

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.710
and YouTube with the hashtag
#askGoogleCloud to be featured

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.310
on a future session.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.790
Stay tuned for more details.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.100
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.050
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.570
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.410
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:01.670
We'll see you in the Cloud.

